### &#xA;Sudan's capital&#x20;

The capital Khartoum is littered with unexploded munitions, according to UN so far 40,000 have been uncovered with only 1% of the city is safely cleared. Below we can see the nightlight differences, then and now. The huge differences in night sky is not good news, another variable in favour of worsening situation.&#x20;

![](https://cdn.metaculus.com/user_uploaded/image_uaEOD4M.png)
Looking at past Famines in Sudan;

I've looked into past three famines in Sudan

|                                                                        | 2017           | 2020          | 2024           |
| ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- | ------------- | -------------- |
| Time spent in emergency (IPC phase 4) before transitioning into Famine | 12 to 14 month | 7 to 8 months | 9 to 10 months |
|                                                                        |                |               |                |

For the current 2026 crisis, areas that remained under IPC phase 4 entered phase 4 in oct/nov 2023, so it's been approx 35 months in phase 4 and that's an extraordinarily prolonged time. It is crucial to notice that the condition is not improving as we have not seen any area to move back into phase 3, which is alarming. They are just one step away from Famine. &#x20;

### &#xA;Conclusion &#x20;

The US push for peace is the silver lining in this conundrum, however to me it seems less likely as the U.S is busy on the other fronts and Sudan is its least of worry on the list. Harvest season is coming but with 14 million displaced people along with total destruction of the land and paired with below average rainfall make things much worse. I think ceasefire beside humanitarian aid is vital to prevent the Famine, if they both occur then the odds should go down, if they don't then I'm afraid, the odds for Famine should rise. I think community has rightly placed it self.

